<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'RDS Database Migration'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>RDS Database Migration</h1>
  <p>Migrated a café app database from EC2-hosted MariaDB to Amazon RDS using mysqldump, with proper networking and Secrets Manager integration.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>RDS</span><span>MariaDB</span><span>Secrets Manager</span><span>EC2</span><span>Database Migration</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/rds-migration.png" alt="RDS Migration Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates migrating a database from <strong>self-managed MariaDB on EC2</strong> to <strong>Amazon RDS</strong> — a fully managed relational database service.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created an <strong>RDS MariaDB instance</strong> with proper VPC networking.</li>
      <li>Verified the existing <strong>café web application</strong> and local database.</li>
      <li>Exported database using <strong>mysqldump</strong> for migration.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>EC2-to-RDS connectivity</strong> via Security Groups.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>Secrets Manager</strong> for secure credential storage.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔴 Before (Self-Managed)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EC2 CafeServer</strong> — Hosts web app</li>
          <li><strong>Local MariaDB</strong> — On same EC2 instance</li>
          <li>Manual backups, patching burden</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🟢 After (Managed RDS)</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>RDS MariaDB</strong> — Managed, automated backups</li>
          <li><strong>Secrets Manager</strong> — Secure credentials</li>
          <li><strong>dbSG</strong> — Port 3306 from EC2 only</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔧 Migration Tools</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>mysqldump</strong> — Export/import data</li>
          <li><strong>Session Manager</strong> — Secure EC2 access</li>
          <li><strong>Subnet Group</strong> — RDS VPC placement</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Understood <strong>self-managed vs managed database</strong> trade-offs.</li>
      <li>Created <strong>RDS instance</strong> with proper VPC and subnet configuration.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>Secrets Manager</strong> for secure credential storage.</li>
      <li>Exported database using <strong>mysqldump</strong> for backup and migration.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>Session Manager</strong> for secure EC2 access without SSH keys.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Always <strong>backup data</strong> before migration using mysqldump or snapshots.</li>
      <li>Enable <strong>Multi-AZ deployment</strong> for production databases.</li>
      <li>Restrict <strong>Security Group rules</strong> to only necessary ports and sources.</li>
      <li>Consider <strong>RDS Proxy</strong> for connection pooling in high-traffic apps.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

